#---
# purpose: "a bitstring size naming a parameter rather than an earlier field is undefined"
# expect: diagnostic
#---
#
# # head_size_pins_nothing
#
# A bitstring field's size may name an earlier field of the same bitstring,
# which binds it before the size is read. Any other name has to have been bound
# before the pattern began, and a `def` head has nothing bound before it. So
# `size(n)` naming a parameter of the same head reaches for a binding that does
# not exist, and Elixir rejects the same head.
def main() do
  dbg(take(2, "hello"))
end

defp take(n, <<s :: binary-size(n), _ :: binary>>), do: s
defp take(_, _), do: :none
